<?xml version="1.0"?>
<model>
  <name>apark_husky</name>
  <version>1.0</version>
  <sdf version="1.9">model.sdf</sdf>
  <author><name>CellularSheaves.jl</name><email>adamkadosh@gmail.com</email></author>
  <description>
    Clearpath Husky A200. The body, top plate and wheels are Clearpath's own
    meshes out of clearpath_platform_description, and the dimensions, masses and
    inertias come from that package's a200.urdf.xacro, so the footprint, the
    0.1651 m wheel radius and the 0.555 m track are the real machine's. Collision
    stays boxes and cylinders. Four wheels are driven, two per side, through the
    one DiffDrive plugin, so the interface the sheaf bridge sees is the Jackal's:
    a Twist in, an Odometry out, same topics.
  </description>
</model>
